# SPI resolution 2026-08-10.mcs.1: Approval of Capital Expenditure for Executive Infrastructure and Data Security

WHEREAS, the President has successfully utilized personal hardware to
manage organizational affairs for approximately twenty (20) years
without organizational expenditure; and

WHEREAS, the President’s personal hardware has recently experienced a
catastrophic and unrecoverable failure, disrupting operational
workflows; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Directors finds it in the best strategic, legal,
and financial interest of Software in the Public Interest, Inc. to
maintain strict digital data segregation between personal and corporate
data to protect institutional intellectual property and donor privacy;
and

WHEREAS, SPI has previously established a precedent for such
infrastructure investments by authorizing a similar hardware expenditure
for SPI Treasurer Héctor Orón Martínez in 2024 within a EUR 1,700 budget
allocation;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the Board of Directors hereby
authorizes a capital expenditure not to exceed $2,200.00 from the SPI
general fund (allowing a small buffer for shifting tax or shipping
rates) for the purchase of an organization- owned ThinkPad T14 Gen 7 AMD
laptop, internal memory/storage upgrades, and an encrypted backup
storage solution for the official use of the President; and

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that this equipment shall remain the sole
property of Software in the Public Interest, Inc., to be maintained on
the corporate asset register, and that the corporate officers are
authorized to take all actions necessary to execute this procurement
effective immediately.
